 "answer": "**Setting up with Fermat's Little Theorem**\n\nSince 163 is prime, Fermat's Little Theorem gives:\n96^162 \u2261 1 (mod 163)\n\nReduce the exponent: 593 mod 162 = 593 \u2212 3(162) = 593 \u2212 486 = 107\n\nSo we need 96^107 mod 163.\n\n**Fast exponentiation (repeated squaring)**\n\n- 96^1 = 96\n- 96^2 = 9216 mod 163 = 88\n- 96^4 = 88\u00b2 = 7744 mod 163 = 83\n- 96^8 = 83\u00b2 = 6889 mod 163 = 43\n- 96^16 = 43\u00b2 = 1849 mod 163 = 56\n- 96^32 = 56\u00b2 = 3136 mod 163 = 39\n- 96^64 = 39\u00b2 = 1521 mod 163 = 54\n\n**Binary decomposition of 107:**  \n107 = 64 + 32 + 8 + 2 + 1\n\nSo:\n96^107 \u2261 96^64 \u00b7 96^32 \u00b7 96^8 \u00b7 96^2 \u00b7 96^1 (mod 163)\n\n**Multiply step by step (mod 163):**\n\n- 54 \u00d7 39 = 2106 \u2192 mod 163 = 150\n- 150 \u00d7 43 = 6450 \u2192 mod 163 = 93\n- 93 \u00d7 88 = 8184 \u2192 mod 163 = 34\n- 34 \u00d7 96 = 3264 \u2192 mod 163 = 4\n\n**Result:** 96^593 \u2261 4 (mod 163)\n\nFINAL: 4"
